<title>SOUTH KOREA: Daewoo wins $220 mln oil tanker order.</title>
<headline>Daewoo wins $220 mln oil tanker order.</headline>
<dateline>SEOUL 1996-12-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>South Korea's Daewoo Heavy Industries Co said on Monday it has won a $220 million contract to build four oil tankers for the U.S-based OMI Corp.  </p>
<p>The 156,000 DWT tankers will be delivered between late 1998 and early 1999, a Daewoo Heavy statement said. confident it could achieve the $2.0 billion shipbuilding order target set for 1996. No further details were given.</p>
<p>-- Seoul Newsroom (822) 727 5643</p>
</text>
